WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:20.307
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is stillness: still water. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.824
Feel where your body meets the chair or floor. Soften your hands. Give gravity permission to carry a little more of your weight.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.427
Feel the quiet rhythm of breathing. When the mind moves ahead, come back to one simple inhale and one unhurried exhale.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:34.031
Stillness is not the absence of movement. It is what a surface does on its own once nothing new is thrown into it. You need only stop stirring.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:02.378
Picture a lake at first light, before any wind. Mountains stand in it, inverted and clear. The water is not holding that picture; it is simply not disturbing it.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:30.031
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:58.495
Find where you are still stirring something. A conversation rehearsed, a decision turned over. Set the stick down and let the water answer for itself.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.356
For a little while, I will be quiet. Let thoughts pass like weather over a wide landscape. When attention wanders, return with patience.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.427
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:28.703
Leave one thing undisturbed today. A pause before you reply. A breath before you open the door. Let stillness be something you allow rather than achieve.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.799
Take one fuller breath. Feel the space beyond your body and let your eyes open in their own time. Thank you for practicing with Karma.
